IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `je54-nouns`
IMPORT `je54-vintage`
IMPORT `je54-art07-service-by-post`

-- je54-tests-art07-service-by-post: Article 7.  Expected values were written from the text of Article 7 before this module was run.
-- The same scenario is put to every one of the seven deposited texts (Article 7 is word for word the same in all seven); the two refusals about the years before 2019 close the module.
-- Scenario: a letter containing the document is properly addressed, prepaid and posted on Friday 1 March 2024; in the ordinary course of post it would be delivered on Monday 4 March 2024 at 09:00.
-- The Law does not say that post takes three days or what the ordinary course of post is: those are the caller's facts.

`text V1` MEANS `V1, 1 January 2019 to 27 September 2021`
`text V2a` MEANS `V2a, 28 September 2021 to 30 January 2022`
`text V2b` MEANS `V2b, 31 January 2022 to 31 August 2022`
`text V2c` MEANS `V2c, 1 September 2022 to 10 January 2024`
`text V2d` MEANS `V2d, 11 January 2024 to 23 November 2025`
`text V2e` MEANS `V2e, 24 November 2025 to 18 June 2026`
`text V2f` MEANS `V2f, 19 June 2026 to current`
`text inferred` MEANS `the inferred text from 28 March 2003 to 31 December 2018`
`text none` MEANS `no text before 28 March 2003`

GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
      mo IS A NUMBER
      d IS A NUMBER
      h IS A NUMBER
      mi IS A NUMBER
      s IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Local moment`
`the local moment` y mo d h mi s MEANS
    `Local moment` WITH
        `calendar day` IS YMD y mo d
        `hour of the day` IS h
        `minute of the hour` IS mi
        `second of the minute` IS s

GIVEN authorized IS A BOOLEAN
      addressed IS A BOOLEAN
      prepaid IS A BOOLEAN
      posted IS A BOOLEAN
      delivery IS A `Local moment`
      proved IS A MAYBE `Local moment`
GIVETH A `Service by post as it happened`
`a letter` authorized addressed prepaid posted delivery proved MEANS
    `Service by post as it happened` WITH
        `the enactment authorizes or requires the document to be served by post` IS authorized
        `the letter was properly addressed` IS addressed
        `the letter was prepaid` IS prepaid
        `the letter was posted` IS posted
        `the time at which the letter would be delivered in the ordinary course of post` IS delivery
        `the other time proved` IS proved

-- the scenario above, and the variants.
`monday morning` MEANS `the local moment` 2024 3 4 9 0 0
`the scenario` MEANS `a letter` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `monday morning` NOTHING

§ `Subsection (1): service is deemed effected by addressing, prepaying and posting`

-- All three acts done, an enactment authorizing service by post, no contrary intention: deemed effected, in each of the seven texts.
#ASSERT `Article 7: service by post is deemed effected` `text V1` `the scenario` FALSE
#ASSERT `Article 7: service by post is deemed effected` `text V2a` `the scenario` FALSE
#ASSERT `Article 7: service by post is deemed effected` `text V2b` `the scenario` FALSE
#ASSERT `Article 7: service by post is deemed effected` `text V2c` `the scenario` FALSE
#ASSERT `Article 7: service by post is deemed effected` `text V2d` `the scenario` FALSE
#ASSERT `Article 7: service by post is deemed effected` `text V2e` `the scenario` FALSE
#ASSERT `Article 7: service by post is deemed effected` `text V2f` `the scenario` FALSE

-- One of the three acts missing: Article 7 does not deem service effected.  (It does not say that service was not effected; it is silent.)
#ASSERT NOT `Article 7: service by post is deemed effected` `text V1` (`a letter` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE `monday morning` NOTHING) FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Article 7: service by post is deemed effected` `text V2c` (`a letter` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE `monday morning` NOTHING) FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Article 7: service by post is deemed effected` `text V2f` (`a letter` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE `monday morning` NOTHING) FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Article 7: service by post is deemed effected` `text V2f` (`a letter` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `monday morning` NOTHING) FALSE

§ `Where Article 7 does not apply`

-- A document served by hand, or by any other mode than post: Article 7 deals only with post.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 7: service by post is deemed effected` `text V1` (`a letter` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE `monday morning` NOTHING) FALSE
        BECAUSE "Article 7 deals only where an enactment authorizes or requires a document to be served by post; it says nothing of any other mode of service"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 7: service by post is deemed effected` `text V2f` (`a letter` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE `monday morning` NOTHING) FALSE
        BECAUSE "Article 7 deals only where an enactment authorizes or requires a document to be served by post; it says nothing of any other mode of service"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 7: the time at which service by post is deemed effected` `text V2c` (`a letter` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE `monday morning` NOTHING) FALSE `the time that is proved`
        BECAUSE "Article 7 deals only where an enactment authorizes or requires a document to be served by post; it says nothing of any other mode of service"

-- A contrary intention appears: the Article does not say what then follows.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 7: service by post is deemed effected` `text V2a` `the scenario` TRUE
        BECAUSE "a contrary intention appears: Article 7 does not say when or whether service by post is then deemed effected"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 7: the time at which service by post is deemed effected` `text V2f` `the scenario` TRUE `the time that is proved`
        BECAUSE "a contrary intention appears: Article 7 does not say when or whether service by post is then deemed effected"

-- The letter was not properly addressed, prepaid and posted: no time, because service is not deemed effected.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 7: the time at which service by post is deemed effected` `text V1` (`a letter` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE `monday morning` NOTHING) FALSE `the time that is proved`
        BECAUSE "service by post is not deemed effected under Article 7 (the letter was not properly addressed, prepaid and posted), so the Article gives no time"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 7: the time at which service by post is deemed effected` `text V2f` (`a letter` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE `monday morning` NOTHING) FALSE `the time that is proved`
        BECAUSE "service by post is not deemed effected under Article 7 (the letter was not properly addressed, prepaid and posted), so the Article gives no time"

§ `Subsection (2): the time at which the letter would be delivered in the ordinary course of post`

-- Nothing proved to the contrary: service is deemed effected at that time (not on the day of posting, Friday 1 March; not on the day of actual receipt).
#ASSERT (`Article 7: the time at which service by post is deemed effected` `text V1` `the scenario` FALSE `the time that is proved`)'s `calendar day` EQUALS YMD 2024 3 4
#ASSERT (`Article 7: the time at which service by post is deemed effected` `text V1` `the scenario` FALSE `the time that is proved`)'s `hour of the day` EQUALS 9
#ASSERT (`Article 7: the time at which service by post is deemed effected` `text V1` `the scenario` FALSE `the time that is proved`)'s `minute of the hour` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT (`Article 7: the time at which service by post is deemed effected` `text V2a` `the scenario` FALSE `the time that is proved`)'s `calendar day` EQUALS YMD 2024 3 4
#ASSERT (`Article 7: the time at which service by post is deemed effected` `text V2b` `the scenario` FALSE `the time that is proved`)'s `calendar day` EQUALS YMD 2024 3 4
#ASSERT (`Article 7: the time at which service by post is deemed effected` `text V2c` `the scenario` FALSE `the time that is proved`)'s `calendar day` EQUALS YMD 2024 3 4
#ASSERT (`Article 7: the time at which service by post is deemed effected` `text V2d` `the scenario` FALSE `the time that is proved`)'s `calendar day` EQUALS YMD 2024 3 4
#ASSERT (`Article 7: the time at which service by post is deemed effected` `text V2e` `the scenario` FALSE `the time that is proved`)'s `calendar day` EQUALS YMD 2024 3 4
#ASSERT (`Article 7: the time at which service by post is deemed effected` `text V2f` `the scenario` FALSE `the time that is proved`)'s `calendar day` EQUALS YMD 2024 3 4

-- The day on which service is deemed effected: the day of the delivery time.  The edge is the stroke of midnight on that clock.
#ASSERT `Article 7: the day on which service by post is deemed effected` `text V2f` `the scenario` FALSE `the time that is proved` EQUALS YMD 2024 3 4
#ASSERT `Article 7: the day on which service by post is deemed effected` `text V2f` (`a letter` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (`the local moment` 2024 3 4 23 59 59) NOTHING) FALSE `the time that is proved` EQUALS YMD 2024 3 4
#ASSERT `Article 7: the day on which service by post is deemed effected` `text V2f` (`a letter` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (`the local moment` 2024 3 5 0 0 0) NOTHING) FALSE `the time that is proved` EQUALS YMD 2024 3 5

§ `The presumption is rebuttable: the contrary is proved (fork I4)`

`saturday afternoon` MEANS `the local moment` 2024 3 2 14 5 0
`a rebutted letter` MEANS `a letter` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `monday morning` (JUST `saturday afternoon`)

-- Reading I4(a), the default: once a different time is proved, that time is the time at which service was effected.
#ASSERT (`Article 7: the time at which service by post is deemed effected` `text V1` `a rebutted letter` FALSE `the time that is proved`)'s `calendar day` EQUALS YMD 2024 3 2
#ASSERT (`Article 7: the time at which service by post is deemed effected` `text V1` `a rebutted letter` FALSE `the time that is proved`)'s `hour of the day` EQUALS 14
#ASSERT (`Article 7: the time at which service by post is deemed effected` `text V1` `a rebutted letter` FALSE `the time that is proved`)'s `minute of the hour` EQUALS 5
#ASSERT (`Article 7: the time at which service by post is deemed effected` `text V2f` `a rebutted letter` FALSE `the time that is proved`)'s `calendar day` EQUALS YMD 2024 3 2
#ASSERT `Article 7: the day on which service by post is deemed effected` `text V2d` `a rebutted letter` FALSE `the time that is proved` EQUALS YMD 2024 3 2

-- Reading I4(b): once the contrary is proved, the Article is silent as to the time.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 7: the time at which service by post is deemed effected` `text V1` `a rebutted letter` FALSE `the Article gives no time`
        BECAUSE "the contrary is proved: on the reading that Article 7 says nothing of the time once the presumption is rebutted, the Article gives no time"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 7: the day on which service by post is deemed effected` `text V2f` `a rebutted letter` FALSE `the Article gives no time`
        BECAUSE "the contrary is proved: on the reading that Article 7 says nothing of the time once the presumption is rebutted, the Article gives no time"
-- With nothing proved the presumption stands on either reading.
#ASSERT (`Article 7: the time at which service by post is deemed effected` `text V2f` `the scenario` FALSE `the Article gives no time`)'s `calendar day` EQUALS YMD 2024 3 4

§ `Before the first consolidated version`

-- No text of Article 7 is deposited for a day before 1 January 2019, and Article 7 is not one of the provisions the inferred row answers (Articles 1(5), 1(6) and the Schedule's "month" and "midnight" only).
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 7: service by post is deemed effected` `text inferred` `the scenario` FALSE
        BECAUSE "before the first consolidated version (1 January 2019)"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 7: the time at which service by post is deemed effected` `text none` `the scenario` FALSE `the time that is proved`
        BECAUSE "before the first consolidated version (1 January 2019)"
